hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27981","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, he said: Marwan sent Abd Allah ibn Utbah to Subayah bint al-Harith, asking her about what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave her as verdict. She informed him that she was under Sad ibn Khawlah, and he died upon her in the Farewell Hajj, and he was a Badri; and she gave birth before four months and ten days of his death elapsed. Abu al-Sanabil, meaning Ibn Bakak, met her when she finished her confinement and had applied kohl, and said to her: Wait for yourself, or the like of this; perhaps you intend marriage; it is four months and ten days from the death of your husband. She said: So I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and mentioned to him what Abu al-Sanabil ibn Bakak said. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to her: You became lawful when you gave birth."
"27982","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us: Rabah narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah wrote to Abd Allah ibn al-Arqam, ordering him to enter upon Subayah bint al-Harith and ask her about what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave her as verdict. She claimed that she was under Sad ibn Khawlah, then he mentioned its meaning."
"27983","Yaqub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from his father, he said: I wrote to Abd Allah ibn al-Arqam, ordering him to enter upon Subayah al-Aslamiyyah and ask her about her affair. He said: He entered upon her, then he mentioned the hadith."
"27984","Yaqub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi narrated to me, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: I entered upon Subayah bint Abi Barzah al-Aslamiyyah and asked her about her affair. She said: I was with Sad ibn Khawlah, and he died upon me, and I remained only two months until I gave birth. She said: Abu al-Sanabil ibn Bakak, the brother of Banu Abd al-Dar, proposed to me, and I prepared for marriage. She said: My in-law entered upon me, while I had dyed and prepared, and said: What do you intend, O Subayah. She said: I said: I intend to marry. He said: By Allah, you have no husband until you wait four months and ten days. She said: So I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and mentioned that to him. He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: You became lawful, so marry."
